1
00:00:00,121 --> 00:00:02,050
You'd expect the cure to be hung up looking

2
00:00:02,110 --> 00:00:04,713
hopeful a light, a flag.

3
00:00:06,183 --> 00:00:07,416
God hung up a snake.

4
00:00:08,727 --> 00:00:09,738
Not a comforting symbol.

5
00:00:10,845 --> 00:00:13,581
The precise shape of their death, lifted up

6
00:00:13,621 --> 00:00:15,062
where the whole camp could see it.

7
00:00:16,429 --> 00:00:19,406
"And Moses made a serpent of brass, and put

8
00:00:19,467 --> 00:00:22,590
it upon a pole, and it came to pass, that if

9
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:26,014
a serpent had bitten any man, when he beheld

10
00:00:26,155 --> 00:00:28,876
the serpent of brass, he lived." Call it too

11
00:00:28,916 --> 00:00:30,178
grim for a cure if you like.

12
00:00:30,707 --> 00:00:32,781
But God never once dressed it up as something

13
00:00:32,882 --> 00:00:33,182
else.

14
00:00:34,032 --> 00:00:35,606
It stayed exactly what it was.

15
00:00:37,436 --> 00:00:39,450
We keep reaching for a gentler version of what

16
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:41,876
Christ did something less costly.

17
00:00:43,144 --> 00:00:44,839
He didn't become a general sacrifice.

18
00:00:45,906 --> 00:00:47,481
He became your curse.

19
00:00:48,928 --> 00:00:51,144
God hung up a snake so the camp could live.

20
00:00:52,171 --> 00:00:56,109
He hung up Christ, His own Son, carrying your

21
00:00:56,269 --> 00:00:58,900
exact curse, so you could too.
